WEBVTT

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.230
Flight members, salute.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.070
At ease.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:15.850
In that stupid game the UN is playing... 
our next opponent will be Argos from Japan.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:16.840
I see.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.580
That's why you're in a good mood.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.950
You can finally avenge yourself 
for the humilation at Kamchatka.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:26.060
Don't worry about the world record 
they won with a ranged-weapon!

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.250
All they did was clear the way for 
the Soviets to do the real work.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.550
Here are our orders from 
United Front Command:

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.910
We are to learn everything there is to know

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.560
about Japan's next-generation TSF, 
so we can be ready, they say.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Since it's an order, we'll have to obey.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.190
But that's less important 
than working off stress.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.320
So she was embarrassed.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.880
Of course I was!

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.390
He wasn't fighting the same 
way we were! It wasn't fair!

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:54.950
I refuse to accept it.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.450
Yuuya Bridges.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.160
I'll see how good you are.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>Pale Blue Flame</b>

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:48.930
A Raptor?

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.190
The Infinities?

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.150
America's quite capable of 
developing its own TSFs.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.030
What are you doing here?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.130
We're going to put an end 
to this waste of time,

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.050
and have everyone here remember 
how important time and money are.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.790
By making them realize how superior American 
TSFs are whether they like it or not.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:17.550
No way... Is America here to shut down the 
XFJ project, no, the Prominence Project itself?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:23.180
I heard that having an Eishi who hates Japan 
was causing the project serious problems.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.070
Wouldn't shutting it down 
be better for the Empire?

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.810
I see you've still got a smart mouth.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.140
I guess you've forgotten all 
the trouble that got you in!

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.260
Sorry.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.300
Alaska's just too cold.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.620
Forget about me.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.240
Keep at it.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.120
This is stupid.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.700
You've had enough?

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.890
See you around, then.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.400
Sorry for interrupting your date.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:02.470
Sharon.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:07.390
Date?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.660
What does she mean?

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.550
She's imagining things. 
Don't worry about it.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.040
No, I mean what is a "date"?

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.230
Oh, well...

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.320
When a man and a woman...

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.910
Cryska! Yuuya!

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:30.410
Inia!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.760
I'm so glad... I was worried you 
wouldn't make it back in time.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.920
I went all kinds of places today.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.880
Jeez, do you know how worried 
Cryska was about yo-

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:42.890
Hey, Yuuya.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.090
Are you going to go away?

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.520
Who is it who lets us drink every day?

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.780
It's Project Chief Lowell!

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.930
Good work today, soldiers of the Empire!

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.790
Tell us, Chief! Go on!

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.510
Thanks to you, the 94 Second's second 
unit is coming together splendidly.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:20.790
And it's all thanks to the amazing 
skills of the Imperial Mechanics!

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.760
Imperial Mechanics are the best in the world!

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.460
Let me rest for a little.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.920
The Japanese are pretty loud when they party.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.750
Can I make something for you?

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.310
Hmm, something refreshing.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.200
Why not a scorpion?

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.560
With no lime.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.160
Yeah, the thing with citrus fruits...

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.620
Are you gonna tell us you can taste 
the pesticides on them again?

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.320
Sharon! Leon!

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.640
What are you doing?

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:54.830
What are you here for?

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.810
The 65th Combat Training Batallion?

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.020
You're with the Infinities now?

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.480
That's a big promotion.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.280
It's been a year or so, hasn't it?

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.310
You look well.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:08.090
Yeah.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.640
I never thought I'd see you here.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.960
It's a small world.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.100
That's right.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:19.180
I never thought I'd see you two 
out here in the middle of nowhere.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:20.100
"Two", huh?

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.410
You met Yuuya too, huh?

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.710
Yeah. He's still an asshole.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:31.130
Nah, he's changed a lot 
since he came to the Yukon.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.370
Like how?

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.950
He's getting along well 
with the Development Team,

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.830
and he's a lot easier to deal with.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:40.320
That's wonderful...

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.330
His new love changed him, didn't it?

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.750
Are you okay?

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:47.240
Love?

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.510
He was just with her.
She was a very elegant woman.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.520
Oh, Princess Yui?

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:58.080
I guess most people would see her that way.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.710
She's not as straight-laced 
as you might think.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:04.650
She's obviously obsessed with him, 
but she doesn't seem to know it.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.440
She's always freaking out when she 
doesn't think anybody's looking.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.350
That's surprising.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:12.280
She felt kind of hard to approach, 
like Yuuya used to be.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.170
Well, her country's always expected 
its soldiers to be pretty stiff.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.760
Lt. Takamura's pushing herself 
pretty hard to live up to that.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.080
Takamura?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.330
She's half-Japanese?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.080
And she was an Ensign.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.830
No, she's pure Japanese.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.360
A Japanese with silver hair?

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.640
That's really rare, isn't it?

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.260
Silver hair?

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:35.930
Elegant.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.720
Hard to approach.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.300
Silver hair?

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.020
Seriously? Again?

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:50.780
You sure you don't mean Ensign Barchenowa?

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:52.450
What?

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.200
So she's one of the Scarlet 
Twins everyone's talking about.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.060
How did you know about her?

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:01.000
Oh, did you forget already?

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.190
Do you think America would send in its 
soldiers without doing the research?

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:07.200
Oh, you're right.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.620
Anyway, Yuuya's not with anybody right now.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:18.720
Then this Takamura's in love with 
him and he doesn't like her?

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.880
I figured she'd be interested in that.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:28.190
Lt. Takamura is in charge of the XFJ plan.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.360
But she doesn't have a lot of 
experience managing things.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:40.750
And so yeah, Yuuya's gotten over 
his whole hate-the-Japanese thing,

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.960
and now he's in love with his new TSF.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.720
Yuuya actually likes Japan?

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:47.960
Unbelievable, right?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:52.350
It wasn't too long ago somebody 
from China asked him what he was,

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:55.630
and he said "Japanese-American" 
without a second thought.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.560
Leon Kuze.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.640
A Japanese-American like me.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.840
He's really changed, hasn't he?

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:08.040
Yeah. He's finally...

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.950
So what?

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.100
Leon.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.570
No matter how much he changes, 
I haven't forgotten what he did,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:15.610
and I haven't forgiven him.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.200
Stop acting like it's over.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.260
Sorry. I'm a little drunk.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:41.470
The most important thing to watch out for is 
the Jian 10's close-range fighting capabilities.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.360
Their primary weapon at close range 
is the Type 77 CIWS.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.630
It's a weapon unique to 
the United Front of China.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:51.480
It's quite different in 
shape than Japan's Type 74.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.980
The biggest difference 
is the center of gravity.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:58.880
The top-heavy shape of the Type 77 
appilies an additional centrifugal force

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.130
to make up for the relative lack of 
strike power that a small TSF has.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:08.380
Thus, the standard method is to defeat 
the enemy with the first strike.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:14.750
That explains why they usually 
strike and then pull back.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.920
Along with the rest of the Eurasian nations,

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.920
I see.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.960
If it was possible for 
Japan to use the Type 77s,

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.640
the United Front of China is 
fighting to take back its homeland.

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:24.400
its strike power would rise
and it would save money on research costs.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.290
Since they are primarily 
intended to take out hives,

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.400
it's only natural that their main TSF

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.450
would be intended for 
short-ranged combat in groups.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:31.650
Hmm... So ideas like that are why
 the UN is making us participate in Blue Flag.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.960
That's all for the TSF's capabilities.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.900
Now tell me what you think, based 
on what you've seen and heard.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.900
Standard theory would call for staying mobile

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.320
and firing from range as opposed 
to getting close, but...

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.410
It's a trap.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.000
They're making them follow standard theory,

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.460
and then that hurricane of a woman starts 
jumping between them and ripping them apart.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:52.960
Clever.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:56.330
We should start with her, definitely.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.310
Got a plan?

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.480
It's simple.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.520
We do the opposite of what they did.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.160
Pretend to play along, and then 
beat them at their own game.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.450
Yuuya!

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.440
Challenge that woman to a duel.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.240
That moron will agree to it, I'm sure.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.240
And then you beat her.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.860
The rest of us will take 
out the other wimpy ones.

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:21.020
Let me just check: are you 
going to use that plan?

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.870
We'll think about it. It can be a backup.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:25.990
What do you mean "backup"?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:30.000
Lt. Dahl, exercises between 
the USSR's Idar Flight

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:34.570
and the Slechtvalk Flight of the 
EU's Benelux Army will begin soon.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:37.450
Alright, everyone to the viewing room.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.560
You're not going to watch, Tarisa?

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.880
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:44.490
Idar's going to win.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.310
No point in going to see it.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:51.680
This exercise is not a mere test 
of our respective capabilities.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.690
It is a demonstration of my Polnoe Zatmeniya plan.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.410
I order you in the name of the Motherland.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:05.700
Show the whole world that submission to us 
is the only way for humanity to survive.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.040
Roger.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.360
Test flights, begin.

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:14.360
It's going alone.

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.010
The other three aren't moving.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.420
They're going to sacrifice that 
one TSF to learn our capabilities?

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:23.120
Let's show them then. 
Surround and destroy them.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.430
Let's send Ivan home crying!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.670
Roger.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.450
I feel a lot better.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.680
There they go.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:46.110
I know it's just CG generated by 
JIVES but it still makes me sick.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.110
So how many are down now?

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:49.210
That's the fourth.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.500
The exercise is over.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:55.710
What do you mean?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.920
It hasn't been 10 minutes.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.910
The Scarlet Twins wiped them out.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.050
And with nothing more than a Motor Blade.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.920
Alone?

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.800
A whole flight of F-16s, 
and the F-16s are faster?

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.460
And in a melee fight in less than 10 minutes?

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.660
This will be fun.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:21.000
If I'm going to perfect the Shiranui, 
I'll need strong opponents.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.640
Come on, let's get back to the briefing.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.720
You can show them up in 
this afternoon's exercises.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.200
Of course! Right, Yuuya?

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.400
Yeah.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.400
So those are the Scarlet Twins 
everyone's talking about?

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.900
Pretty impressive.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.720
You sure?

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.090
If you don't let them get 
close they can't hurt you.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.660
You're not really interested, are you?

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:53.100
Were you so busy thinking about this 
afternoon's match that you weren't paying attention?

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:55.600
Say what you like.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:58.490
That joint US-Japan TSF?

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:01.230
They're going to be using their second one 
without giving the pilot any time to train.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:05.360
They won't be working as 
well as an element, though.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.560
They're prioritizing the development 
schedule above everything else, huh?

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.370
I don't know if that's a smart idea or not.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:15.620
But the bookies here have 
Argos as the dark horse.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.620
Then what about us?

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:22.840
We're so sure to win they aren't taking bets.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:40.750
There was between a .2-.3 drop 
in reaction speed and firing accuracy.

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:42.490
Was there a problem with the TSF?

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.440
None found at the moment.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.870
Hurry with the inspection.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:52.700
Yes sir.

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:59.930
Listen, the basic movement 
data is copied from number 1.

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.950
It'll move very different from how it feels.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:04.780
Sorry, but you'll just have to 
get used to it during the fight.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.170
Leave it to me.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:09.590
Doing the impossible is 
part of a test pilot's job.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.350
Argos 1, launching.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.440
Ensign Bridges.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.430
I'm counting on you.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:26.320
Roger.

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.450
Bao Feng 1 to all flight members.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:40.450
You know the drill, right?

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:45.050
Let's pay them back for Kamchatka.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.090
Roger!

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:53.470
I'm glad to have another melee fight.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:55.970
That feeling I almost mastered back there...

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.850
I'm going to test it here.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:02.600
Both Test Flights have 
arrived at the start points.

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:04.250
On time.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.390
Begin the exercise!

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:09.690
So there was no problem 
with the machine, then?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.160
Which means...

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.110
Yes, the next thing to do is look 
for problems with synchronization.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:15.340
That's...

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.380
Yuuya!

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:26.640
You have permission to 
use the Adjustment Tanks.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.350
Doctor, find what's causing 
this as soon as possible.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:31.630
Yes sir.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:42.600
Damn it!

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:44.250
Yuuya!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:49.730
These tiny little differences 
are annoying me!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.330
Where are you looking?

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:04.540
Why you...

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:05.830
They're just screwing with us!

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:07.180
No, Argos 1!

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:08.830
You're letting the decoys 
move you around too much!

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:12.030
The enemy is functioning 
far better as a team,

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:14.590
but I'm not sure I understand 
what's happening.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:18.340
It's like the Bao Feng Flight has no 
intention of finishing the battle.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:23.200
This is a pain!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.340
The Japanese TSFs don't 
handle like anything else!

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:27.560
They're just playing with us.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:31.130
One of ours is just slowing us 
down, at this rate we're doomed.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.080
Who's just slowing us down?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.900
We'll have to go with the backup plan.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.120
This is supposed to be a real fight.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.880
A duel doesn't make sense.

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.000
They won't agree to it.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.080
No, they're trying to draw me out.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.570
We'll do what Tarisa suggested.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:48.400
We'll beat them on their own gruond.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.790
That's him. Argos 1.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.130
He's finally come out, huh?

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:56.520
Everyone split up, and don't 
let the weaker ones interfere.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:57.380
Roger!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.870
Here I come, Yuuya Bridges!

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:12.700
What?

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:23.640
How stupid.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.460
I knew it.

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:34.670
That's just what I wanted.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:37.670
Wonderful... you're wonderful!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.640
She's hitting hard!

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:55.130
Take this!

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:57.310
Is that all you've got?

00:18:57.980 --> 00:18:59.450
Don't disappoint me!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.000
This strength.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.450
It's not just her blade.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.550
Combined Tension! {This is a made up word for muv-luv. In fact, it only appears in regards to this mech.}

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:10.120
She's using all the carbonic 
actuators in her TSF like a whip!

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.210
Bridges!

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:16.590
Damn it!

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:17.960
What is she doing?

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.730
She keeps pushing me back.

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:22.840
So why doesn't she finish me?

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.690
Is she playing with me?

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.010
No, she's not.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:29.450
I see.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.420
So that's it.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.480
Thanks, Lt. Cui.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:36.800
I guess you're ready.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:41.610
Then I'll end it here, Yuuya Bridges!

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:49.340
What?

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.160
Sorry, Lieutenant!

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.090
No you don't!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.840
I can turn my blade around faster.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.770
He was losing the whole time, I'm 
amazed he managed to come back.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:19.800
The bookies are going to lose a fortune.

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.430
Yuuya won, didn't he?

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:34.400
It was just like I said, wasn't it?

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:40.510
It's a shame we didn't take out 
the other 3, but a win is a win.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.970
They all withdrew when 
their leader went down.

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:45.920
It was like they let us win, wasn't it?

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:50.970
It may be they're not interested in 
who wins, or in Blue Flag at all.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.910
I know I felt it there.

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.940
Have I finally mastered that feeling?

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.230
Ensign Bridges.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:01.660
Lieutenant?

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.290
That was a splendid strike.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:08.170
You brought the Shiranui 
2 to its full potential.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:08.990
Thank you.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.210
I wanted to tell you that.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:15.120
No, I was stupid.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:20.250
I thought that the Japanese blades were 
defective, with a bad center of gravity.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:27.510
But in that last battle I realized that its 
center of gravity was perfect for multiple strikes.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:29.740
To be honest, I'm amazed.

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:33.270
Whatever Japanese engineer 
designed that was a genius.

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:36.510
Hey, Lieutenant.

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:38.360
I have a request for you.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:40.320
For me?

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:42.860
Yeah. You're the only one I can ask.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:45.860
I'm the only one-

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:50.110
There's Yuuya!

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.120
Lt. Cui!

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:57.210
Hey, wai-

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:05.510
Yuuya Bridges!

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:08.880
You can fall in love with me if you want.

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:18.890
Well, Doctor?

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.040
It's inexplicable.

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:22.900
Synchronization error is 
within acceptable parameters.

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:25.320
And their vital data is fine as well.

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:28.900
Which means...

00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:12.280
Whenever I think about 
you, I can't concentrate.

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:15.360
It's going to start affecting my mission.

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:17.510
And before it does I need to find out why!

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:24.350
<b>Dark Recollection</b>

00:24:19.360 --> 00:24:21.550
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:23.950
Dark Recollection
